`tessera info` — what this build is (ADR-0057 §7). The shape is pinned here; the *semantics*
(build modes tracking `cfg!`, JSON keys, the disabled set) are pinned by the unit tests in
`src/info.rs`. Versions are wildcarded because a dependency bump must not break a docs walkthrough.

```
$ tessera info
tessera [..]
backends:   arrow 58.3.0 · blob · blob-series · csv 1.4.0 · dicom 0.10.0 · dicom-series 0.10.0 · hdf-compound 1.14.6 · nifti · npy · npz-member 2.4.2 · parquet 58.3.0 · raw
disabled:   (none)
build:      static-hdf5=[..] · cloud=[..] · sql=[..]

```

Nothing is disabled in a default build: `arrow`, `parquet` and `csv` are feature-gated (ADR-0057 §5)
but default-ON, because the gates exist for embedders and CI, not for end users — a downloaded
`tessera` that cannot read Parquet is a bad binary. Build with `--no-default-features` and those three
names move to the `disabled:` line instead of vanishing, which is what lets an ingest naming one fail
with "not compiled into this build" (exit 3) rather than "unknown backend" (exit 2).

`--json` emits the same facts in a shape meant for `aux/provenance.json`. The binary flavor is
deliberately NOT sealed: ADR-0056 §6a seals the `ingest_decoder` triple, which is what actually
determined the bytes. ADR-0042's line holds — sealed = what changed the bytes; `aux/` = who was in the
room.

It also carries, **per ingest lane**, the sealed feature digest and the **pre-image** it is taken over — one entry per lane since #477, because a global digest made a parquet product commit to the crate list of every other lane. The pre-image is `v2;`-prefixed: the derivation is versioned, so a future change to it reads as a declared difference rather than as a decoder that moved. Alongside the
digest itself, so the third component of that triple is checkable rather than merely observable: a
reader holding a `.tsra` and this output from the same version can confirm the correspondence.

```
$ tessera info --json
{
  "tessera_version": "[..]",
  "format_version": "[..]",
  "backends": [
    {
      "name": "arrow",
      "version": "[..]"
    },
    {
      "name": "blob"
    },
    {
      "name": "blob-series"
    },
    {
      "name": "csv",
      "version": "[..]"
    },
    {
      "name": "dicom",
      "version": "[..]"
    },
    {
      "name": "dicom-series",
      "version": "[..]"
    },
    {
      "name": "hdf-compound",
      "version": "[..]"
    },
    {
      "name": "nifti"
    },
    {
      "name": "npy"
    },
    {
      "name": "npz-member",
      "version": "2.4.2"
    },
    {
      "name": "parquet",
      "version": "58.3.0"
    },
    {
      "name": "raw"
    }
  ],
  "backends_disabled": [],
  "build": {
    "cloud": false,
    "sql": false,
    "static-hdf5": false
  },
  "ingest_decode": {
    "arrow-rs/arrow-ipc": {
      "digest": "blake3:[..]",
      "features": "v2;pins=[..]"
    },
    "arrow-rs/parquet": {
      "digest": "blake3:[..]",
      "features": "v2;pins=[..]"
    },
    "rust-csv": {
      "digest": "blake3:[..]",
      "features": "v2;pins=[..]"
    },
    "tessera/npy": {
      "in_tree": true
    },
    "tessera/npz": {
      "digest": "blake3:[..]",
      "features": "v2;pins=[..]"
    }
  }
}

```
